:: Carter Connor Part 3 [nobr]

/* Intro */
<<set $Minutes += 30>>
You and <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span> spend a long time just chatting, so long in fact that, <span style="Color: Yellow">when you suddenly realize the time,</span> <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span> quickly blushes and begins apologizing. <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Sorry, sorry, sorry!”</span> He says, <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“I didn’t mean to keep you out here so long, we’ve almost missed all of first period… I just got talking and-! I’ll make sure they know it was my fault! We’ll say I dragged you here by force, or-!”</span> <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span> suddenly pauses, <span style="Color: Yellow">looking past you with a shocked expression.</span> As you turn around, you hear a female voice softly ask. <br>

        <<set _ad to [
            {
                Name: "Player",
                State: {
                    Mouth: "Frown",
                    BlusH: 1,
                },
            },
            {
                Name: "Carter",
                State: {
                    Outfit: "Uniform",
                    Mouth: "Frown",
                    Blush: 2,
                    Cry: 1,
                },
            },
        ]>>
        <<ad _ad>>

<span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Mind if I join you two?”</span> <span style="Color: Yellow">You turn to see <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span>’s mom, her hair a bit of a mess and her eyes with dark bags under them.</span> She is holding a bag and some blue flowers. You then look at <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span>, who seems just as surprised and unsure as you are, before slowly nodding. <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“I figured you may be here. We got a call from the school that you didn’t show up to class, someone saw you leaving. Normally, they would have just thought you were ditching class but- Well, your headmaster knows you well.”</span> <br>
<br>
<span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“S- sorry… I know I should have asked or something, but…”</span> <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span> looks down, staring at the grass as his mom walks up, <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“It isn’t <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">$CarterNickname</span>’s fault! I forced him to-!”</span> <br>
<br>
<span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“It’s fine.”</span> She steps up to the grave, staring at <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span> rather than the stone, before taking a deep breath and looking straight at it. <span style="Color: LightCoral">It looks like it hurts.</span> <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Do you mind if I sit with you a little bit? I… I thought it might be good to be with the real <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Connor</span> for once.”</span> You notice <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span> bit his lip, nervous and unsure what to say. When neither of you respond she just simply sits down at the grave, placing the flowers down. <span style="Color: Yellow">The three of you then just sit in silence for a moment. It’s awkward, at first, but things slowly ease and both of your muscles relax.</span> <br>
<br>
<span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“I’m sorry I missed your award ceremony.”</span> She finally speaks, hurt in her voice, <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“I… I want to say I tried, that I wanted to go, because I really, really did. But I know just trying isn’t enough. It’s okay if you’re mad at me, it’s-”</span> <br>
<br>
<span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“I’m not mad!”</span> <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span> quickly interrupts, <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“I- I know it’s not your fault… I was just… I don’t know. It just isn’t fair. You’re the one who’s sick, who’s dealing with it. It’s not fair to blame you.”</span> <br>
<br>
<span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Even if it isn’t my fault, I’m sorry.”</span> There is another long pause, before she speaks. <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“You and your brother were perfect. Different, but… perfect in your own ways. He was such a little troublemaker, always escaping his crib or moving his veggies to your plate to pretend he ate them. He was also pretty tough, physically anyway. The two of you used to run around, tripping and falling all the time and running into anything that wasn’t nailed down, but he’d always get up with little more than a tear. But even though he was tough, he was sensitive. He used to cry when you’d gone down for your nap without him or when your dad was working late and couldn’t tuck him in. We tried to get you guys to sleep in separate cribs, but he somehow always ended up in yours by morning. We never figured out how he did it.”</span> She chuckles, causing you and <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span> to as well. <br>

