    <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“I love you too…”</span> <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span> replies through his tears and running nose, <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“and I always will, whether you get better someday or… not.”</span> She looks down and smiles at her son. She knows she still hurt him, it’s clear in her eyes, and she can never truly make up for everything. <span style="Color: Pink">But she looks determined, she won’t stop trying. They both seem to remember you are there and chuckle nervously, his mother wiping her eyes as <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span> smiles nervously, a little embarrassed but happy you are here to support him. He then picks up the award and looks at it, smiling widely. His mom looks down at the award too as <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span> runs his finger along the spots that have been glued back together.</span> <br>
    <br>
    <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“The cracks are still visible, and it might be missing a piece or two, but… You deserve this and so much more. I want to say I’ll be different, that things will be better, that I’ll always be here, but… the truth is I may slip again, I probably will. I’m… not better now, maybe I never will be. But no matter how far I fall or how cloudy everything gets, I will never stop trying and fighting to get back to you all. And I will never hide the truth to you again, even if that truth hurts. You deserve to know… everything about <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Connor</span>. Any question about <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Connor</span>, the real <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Connor</span>, or my disease or… anything. I’ll answer, whenever you have them.”</span> <br>
    <br>
    <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“I… I do have one question.”</span> <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span> says softly, <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“I… I always wondered what his favorite thing to play with was. Was it his bear… or-?”</span> <br>
    <br>
    <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“He did love that bear.”</span> She laughs, <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“But it wasn’t his favorite thing in the world. Whenever he saw his favorite thing, he’d drop his bear and just take off running to it.”</span> <br>
    <br>
    <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“What was it?”</span> <br>
    <br>
    <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“It was you.”</span> <br>
    <br>
    <<linkreplace"Continue">>
        The three of you sit there for a while longer in silence before his mom stands up, saying she should get you both back to school before you miss too many classes. She gives you both a lift back, the entire car ride being quiet. But it isn’t quiet like it was before. It isn’t an awkward silence filled with unspoken words or resentment. <span style="Color: Yellow">Instead, they both just seem lost in thought.</span> As the car pulls up to the school, <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span> turns to his mom before getting out. <br>
        <br>
        <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Mom?”</span> He says nervously, <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Thank you for telling me about <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Connor</span>. It’s sad, but… I’m glad I know. Do… do you think we could talk about him more after school?”</span> <br>
        <br>
        <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Of course.”</span> She smiles, <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“I would love that.”</span> <br>
        <br>
        <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span> smiles as the two of you walk inside, finding <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Headmaster Alistair</span> waiting for you. He scolds you both for skipping class, <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span> taking the blame as he said he would, but you surprisingly don’t get any detention. <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Alistair</span> <span style="Color: Pink">makes it clear this is a one time thing, that next time you try to skip he’ll bend you both over his knee himself.</span> Right before sending you both to class, <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Alistair</span> stops <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span> and asks <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Are you okay?”</span> <br>
        <br>
        <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“I… don’t know. But I will be.”</span> <span style="Color: Pink">He gives a big smile, putting his arm around you,</span> <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Especially with <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">$CarterNickname</span> here!”</span> And with that, the two of you head off to your first class, or what's left of it anyway. <br>
        <span style="color:Gold">Quest Complete: "Carter: Connor"!</span><br>
